WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:24.890 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.399 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily closing price is

00:00:27.399 --> 00:00:28.931 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the last price of that day.

00:00:29.451 --> 00:00:31.525 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:33.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily prices, marked Example.

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:36.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.908 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

00:00:40.428 --> 00:00:42.562 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A range is the top and the bottom,

00:00:42.562 --> 00:00:44.942 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two lines,

00:00:44.942 --> 00:00:47.241 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:47.761 --> 00:00:49.799 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.692 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the range.

00:00:52.212 --> 00:00:54.111 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:54.111 --> 00:00:56.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:56.935 --> 00:00:58.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:00.382 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:01.582 --> 00:01:03.873 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.725 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:08.457 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:09.565 --> 00:01:11.729 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook,

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:14.153 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, range, levels and stop,

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:16.404 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the pair, paper or a demo account,

00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:18.481 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
no secrets, a written stop, and

00:01:18.481 --> 00:01:20.818 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the word Example on every figure.

00:01:21.338 --> 00:01:22.719 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:23.239 --> 00:01:24.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.697 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you drawing

00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:28.911 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a grid with no edges.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.789 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you buy

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:32.018 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and what you pay with.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.856 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:33.856 --> 00:01:35.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.089 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:38.582 --> 00:01:40.313 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:40.606 --> 00:01:42.394 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:44.173 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair

00:01:44.173 --> 00:01:45.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:46.471 --> 00:01:48.664 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:49.184 --> 00:01:50.643 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily closing price is

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.101 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the last price of the day.

00:01:52.622 --> 00:01:54.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:54.074 --> 00:01:55.638 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.182 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:58.587 --> 00:02:01.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:01.692 --> 00:02:03.716 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:03.716 --> 00:02:05.665 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:06.185 --> 00:02:08.552 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:08.552 --> 00:02:10.619 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:12.798 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:13.231 --> 00:02:15.310 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.537 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if a daily closing price finishes

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.764 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside the range and the next daily

00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:21.694 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closing price is still outside.

00:02:22.214 --> 00:02:24.034 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:24.034 --> 00:02:25.703 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:26.223 --> 00:02:27.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the

00:02:27.899 --> 00:02:30.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:31.004 --> 00:02:33.126 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:33.443 --> 00:02:35.342 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:35.342 --> 00:02:36.749 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:38.666 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:38.666 --> 00:02:40.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:43.366 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:46.079 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account,

00:02:46.079 --> 00:02:48.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and sometimes move money out of it.

00:02:49.131 --> 00:02:51.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:51.943 --> 00:02:54.483 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:55.003 --> 00:02:56.801 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:57.322 --> 00:02:58.643 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public closing price

00:02:58.643 --> 00:02:59.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is not your account.

00:03:00.276 --> 00:03:01.907 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:03:01.907 --> 00:03:03.693 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:04.743 --> 00:03:06.716 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the range onto the page,

00:03:06.716 --> 00:03:08.159 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not every day's prices.

00:03:08.679 --> 00:03:10.913 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:10.913 --> 00:03:13.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:15.575 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every closing price in that window

00:03:15.575 --> 00:03:16.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the range.

00:03:17.529 --> 00:03:18.931 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:19.981 --> 00:03:21.598 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, range,

00:03:21.598 --> 00:03:23.052 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:23.572 --> 00:03:25.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with no

00:03:25.787 --> 00:03:27.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily closing

00:03:30.724 --> 00:03:32.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price finishes outside the range

00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:35.032 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily closing price

00:03:35.032 --> 00:03:37.382 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is still outside, the example is over.

00:03:38.432 --> 00:03:40.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:42.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:45.381 --> 00:03:46.890 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:48.843 --> 00:03:50.137 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:50.657 --> 00:03:52.054 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:54.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:55.491 --> 00:03:57.558 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:57.907 --> 00:03:59.751 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:04:00.134 --> 00:04:01.613 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:04:01.613 --> 00:04:03.021 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:05.664 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:06.789 --> 00:04:07.962 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:09.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:10.263 --> 00:04:11.995 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:12.329 --> 00:04:15.504 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the July

00:04:15.504 --> 00:04:18.579 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window, the public

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:21.555 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closing prices from 19 July

00:04:21.555 --> 00:04:24.531 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to 16 October 2023, so you buy the base,

00:04:24.531 --> 00:04:27.309 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

00:04:27.309 --> 00:04:29.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:30.507 --> 00:04:32.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:32.741 --> 00:04:34.322 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We price in US dollars.

00:04:34.842 --> 00:04:36.594 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your exchange may charge fees

00:04:36.594 --> 00:04:38.066 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars, so

00:04:38.066 --> 00:04:39.630 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
keep each in its own column.

00:04:40.128 --> 00:04:42.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:42.304 --> 00:04:44.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:47.081 --> 00:04:48.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and

00:04:48.987 --> 00:04:51.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:52.553 --> 00:04:55.138 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:55.894 --> 00:05:00.376 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the July to October example window

00:05:00.873 --> 00:05:04.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:05:04.579 --> 00:05:05.976 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.379 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:05:08.669 --> 00:05:10.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:05:10.828 --> 00:05:12.826 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:05:15.202 --> 00:05:17.213 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:05:17.646 --> 00:05:19.773 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you got

00:05:19.773 --> 00:05:21.505 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:21.505 --> 00:05:23.395 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:24.445 --> 00:05:25.715 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has

00:05:25.715 --> 00:05:27.056 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to say what you will do.

00:05:27.506 --> 00:05:29.313 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places

00:05:29.313 --> 00:05:31.723 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:32.243 --> 00:05:34.319 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closing prices outside

00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:35.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, through the top

00:05:35.876 --> 00:05:37.582 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or the bottom, and the second

00:05:37.582 --> 00:05:39.361 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closing price still outside.

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:41.445 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:41.445 --> 00:05:43.033 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders,

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.232 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:48.194 --> 00:05:50.924 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:50.924 --> 00:05:53.421 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:53.941 --> 00:05:55.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:55.957 --> 00:05:57.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:58.277 --> 00:06:00.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.512 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and

00:06:02.512 --> 00:06:04.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the exchange runs it, not this course.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.264 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:06:07.264 --> 00:06:09.119 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:11.706 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:06:11.706 --> 00:06:13.270 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:06:13.531 --> 00:06:16.073 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services

00:06:16.073 --> 00:06:18.692 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:18.692 --> 00:06:21.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:21.312 --> 00:06:23.623 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:24.143 --> 00:06:25.407 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:25.407 --> 00:06:26.748 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:27.259 --> 00:06:29.437 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.201 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:32.628 --> 00:06:34.862 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:35.142 --> 00:06:37.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:38.257 --> 00:06:40.187 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:40.187 --> 00:06:41.449 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:44.910 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, platforms that hold

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:47.754 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto for you need an ASIC licence,

00:06:47.754 --> 00:06:50.695 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a transition period to October

00:06:50.695 --> 00:06:53.832 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2027 for platforms already operating.

00:06:54.352 --> 00:06:56.363 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:58.591 --> 00:07:00.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:07:01.075 --> 00:07:03.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your password,

00:07:03.312 --> 00:07:05.189 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is two-factor authentication.

00:07:05.709 --> 00:07:07.809 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:07:08.329 --> 00:07:10.363 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:07:10.949 --> 00:07:12.470 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:07:15.661 --> 00:07:17.169 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is when your waiting

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.456 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order actually trades.

00:07:18.976 --> 00:07:21.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:07:21.267 --> 00:07:23.389 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:23.599 --> 00:07:25.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:25.275 --> 00:07:27.007 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:27.344 --> 00:07:29.042 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:29.042 --> 00:07:30.741 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:31.261 --> 00:07:32.713 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:32.713 --> 00:07:34.166 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:34.574 --> 00:07:37.397 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:37.917 --> 00:07:40.997 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:40.997 --> 00:07:43.758 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:44.278 --> 00:07:46.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:46.722 --> 00:07:48.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:48.566 --> 00:07:50.498 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:51.018 --> 00:07:53.056 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:53.576 --> 00:07:54.638 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the July

00:07:54.638 --> 00:07:56.308 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window.

00:07:56.828 --> 00:07:59.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:59.139 --> 00:08:01.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:08:01.616 --> 00:08:04.257 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:08:04.777 --> 00:08:06.732 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
To compare them, turn the gap into

00:08:06.732 --> 00:08:08.904 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a percent by dividing it by the price.

00:08:09.424 --> 00:08:12.421 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the lesson 1 example, 900

00:08:12.421 --> 00:08:15.827 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by 27,630 is about 3.3

00:08:15.827 --> 00:08:19.369 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, well above 0.2 percent.

00:08:19.889 --> 00:08:21.433 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:22.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:08:23.277 --> 00:08:25.344 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:08:25.977 --> 00:08:27.863 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin built

00:08:27.863 --> 00:08:30.077 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay worth about one US dollar.

00:08:30.597 --> 00:08:32.217 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:08:32.685 --> 00:08:35.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If your pair is priced in a stablecoin,

00:08:35.139 --> 00:08:37.671 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill trades one coin for another,

00:08:37.671 --> 00:08:39.096 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every fill is a swap.

00:08:40.146 --> 00:08:42.351 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated record

00:08:42.351 --> 00:08:43.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of every bot: the plan,

00:08:43.644 --> 00:08:45.545 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the changes, the fills, the fees,

00:08:45.545 --> 00:08:47.446 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a review note of what happened,

00:08:47.446 --> 00:08:49.651 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and whether you followed the rules.

00:08:50.171 --> 00:08:51.959 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:52.308 --> 00:08:54.442 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:54.962 --> 00:08:57.274 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

00:08:57.274 --> 00:08:59.225 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every swap goes in the journal.

00:08:59.745 --> 00:09:02.030 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is also the page you will

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:09:04.759 --> 00:09:07.284 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:09:07.284 --> 00:09:09.336 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

00:09:09.336 --> 00:09:11.783 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the value

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:13.993 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars at the time,

00:09:13.993 --> 00:09:16.439 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

00:09:16.439 --> 00:09:18.728 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it was for, and who the other side was.

00:09:19.248 --> 00:09:21.322 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:09:21.322 --> 00:09:23.089 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, the gaps, the money

00:09:23.089 --> 00:09:24.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in the bot, the stop rule,

00:09:24.548 --> 00:09:26.699 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fills, the fees, the Australian

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:28.850 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar value of each fill, a review

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:09:31.367 --> 00:09:33.004 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The Australian dollar value

00:09:33.004 --> 00:09:34.573 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column is the one exception.

00:09:35.093 --> 00:09:36.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is for your tax records.

00:09:37.119 --> 00:09:39.222 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:09:39.222 --> 00:09:41.233 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:09:41.654 --> 00:09:42.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.001 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for at least five years.

00:09:44.357 --> 00:09:46.129 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:09:46.129 --> 00:09:47.015 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:09:47.535 --> 00:09:49.323 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:49.742 --> 00:09:50.905 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:51.425 --> 00:09:53.716 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.023 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:55.472 --> 00:09:57.316 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:57.977 --> 00:10:00.367 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask

00:10:00.367 --> 00:10:02.315 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for a seed phrase, a private

00:10:02.315 --> 00:10:03.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret.

00:10:04.251 --> 00:10:06.227 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:10:06.227 --> 00:10:07.650 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, or asks for one

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:09.310 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of those, treat it as a scam.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:10:12.071 --> 00:10:14.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:10:14.566 --> 00:10:16.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:10:17.287 --> 00:10:18.293 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:10:19.283 --> 00:10:21.587 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now cover the chart and say your page

00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:23.276 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
out loud: the pair, the range,

00:10:23.276 --> 00:10:24.889 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the stop rule.

00:10:25.409 --> 00:10:27.410 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.103 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:10:29.623 --> 00:10:31.743 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:10:31.743 --> 00:10:33.863 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:10:34.383 --> 00:10:36.488 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase,

00:10:36.488 --> 00:10:39.015 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a private key, or an API secret.

00:10:39.535 --> 00:10:41.211 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:10:41.609 --> 00:10:43.846 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own notebook

00:10:43.846 --> 00:10:45.874 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so a practice sketch is never later

00:10:45.874 --> 00:10:47.272 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
mistaken for a live plan.

00:10:48.322 --> 00:10:50.702 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:10:50.702 --> 00:10:52.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:52.843 --> 00:10:55.144 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:56.344 --> 00:10:57.758 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: How a grid

00:10:57.758 --> 00:10:59.329 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot works, order by order.

00:10:59.849 --> 00:11:01.469 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your range,

00:11:01.469 --> 00:11:03.089 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:11:03.331 --> 00:11:04.553 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example

00:11:04.553 --> 00:11:05.979 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on every practice figure.

00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:08.147 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:11:08.147 --> 00:11:09.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

